Resolutions
10. Consideration of a resolution setting county officials salaries for the
years 2027-2030.
25 - 566
Salaries County Officials 2027-2030
Attachments:
Chairman Malm opened the meeting for PUBLIC COMMENT.  Todd Ernst, Assessor,
spoke on behalf of the other elected officials.  He said that this is the first pay
adjustment since 2018, and Laramie County elected officials have fallen below some
of the other counties, even though we are the most populous and complex in the state.
He said that under compensation creates the risk of less effective, accountable, and
transparent government by significantly limiting the pool of qualified individuals willing
to run for office. He stated that this decision is an important step to ensuring strong
leadership, responsibility and governance. Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT,
Chairman Malm closed the comment period.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, that this agenda item be approved. The
motion carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
Aye:
