### Page 5 of 5

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
December 2, 2025
Public Hearings/Rules & Reg’s
14. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a resolution to amend the 2024
International Residential Code, Section R105.2 Work exempt from
permit.
25 - 560
Resolution, Amending the 2024 Int'l Residential Code
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said the purpose of the amendment is to change the current
square foot exemption for detached accessory structures from 200 square feet to 400
square feet.  The recommended changes will exempt shipping containers, sheds, and
small carports from building permits.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT.  Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Zwonitzer, to amend the 2024 International Residential
Code Section 105.2-Work Exempt from Permit and is hereby amended to
read as follows: Building: 1. To read "Other than storm shelters, one-story
detached accessory structures, provided that the floor area does not
exceed 400 square feet. The motion carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
Aye:
The meeting adjourned at 3:51 pm.
CERTIFICATION
I, Debra K. Lee, Clerk of Laramie County, do hereby certify the above to be a true
and correct copy of the Minutes of the Proceedings for Tuesday, Dec 2, 2025.
Approved by : Debra K. Lee, County Clerk
Reviewed by : Gunnar Malm, Chairman,
Board of County Commissioners
Reasonable Accommodations
This information is available in alternate forms.  If reasonable accommodations are
required, contact Laramie County Human Resources at (307) 633-4355 or
humanresources@laramiecountywy.gov at least two business days prior to the
meeting. Per WS §18-3-516(f), access to county information can be obtained at
laramiecountywy.gov.
